e":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nv4.4.stable.official [4c311cbee]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.stable - macOS Sequoia (15.3.1) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Metal (Forward+) - integrated Apple M2 (Apple8) - Apple M2 (8 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen specifying `@export_range` for a float value, Godot suggested I put one of the specialized string options (`\"or_greater\"`, etc.) on 3rd argument. I thought that was odd, since _I know_ there is supposed to be a `step` as a third argument. So I placed my _step_ in front of the suggested string and it really errored!\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a1c5ec19-feb4-4086-acc6-b095641b72d5)\n\nI think this is just the editor's wrong suggestion. Docs are clear on this, extra hints should come from 4th place onward.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Start typing `@export_range(0.0, 10.0, `\n- Wait for completion to trigger\n- String option will be suggested, which it shouldn't be, as this is the place for `step` parameter, not `extra_hints`\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nEasy enough to reproduce","closed_by":{"login":"VojtaStruhar","id":49688205,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5Njg4MjA1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49688205?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/VojtaStruhar","html_url":"https://github.com/VojtaStruhar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VojtaStruhar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VojtaStruhar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VojtaStruhar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VojtaStruhar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vojt